  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Monterey College of Law 'JD Graduation Checklist — Classes of 2030 and beyond (first enrolled after September 1, 2025)' (montereylaw.edu/currentstudent/JDGraduationChecklistClassof2030.pdf). Empire College (Santa Rosa) discontinued its School of Business in 2020; in July 2022 its School of Law became 'Empire College of Law, a branch of Monterey College of Law,' teaching MCL's curriculum at the Santa Rosa campus (Committee of Bar Examiners major-change approval; montereylaw.edu). The JD is the branch's currently offered law degree. Required sequence sums: 1L 10+11+5=26, 2L 10+10+2=22, 3L 10+6+2=18, 4L 6+3=9; required 75 units. The checklist's summary box confirms: 1L 26 + 2L 22 + 3L 18 + 4L 9 = 75 required; General Clinical 2 + Core Mediation 2 + General Elective 11 = 15; 90 total units. (The checklist's intro prose says 'seventy required units' — stale text; the per-course and summary-box figures, 75 required / 90 total, are used.) MCL publishes JD courses by name (no separate course numbers), so official course names serve as codes. Clinical & Elective requirements are not term-sequenced in the checklist; they are modeled as choice slots in the final term with the checklist's scheduling guidance quoted in each choice_note. Per-course prerequisites are published in the MCL JD Course Catalog; prereq arrays are intentionally empty and the published required order is the prerequisite-respecting order.",
